<?xml version="1.0"?>
<CP_Scriptfile date="Feb 20, 2023">
<CPscript title="Flip Challenge with the Soccer42 combinatorics" level="min" >
<description>Your goal: flip edges to convert the given packing into the one pictured here. The 42 circles are colored according to degree. Press 'f' on an edge that you want to flip: the packing will be recomputed, color coded, and redisplayed. As a first stage, try to get all circles to be white (degree 6) or blue (degree 5). Enjoy! (Copyright: Ken Stephenson)</description>
<text> Your goal is the circle packing pattern of a regular dodecahedron --- basically, of a soccer ball. Throughout this script the circles will be color-coded by degree; for example, degree 5 (5 neighbors) is blue and degree 6 is white. 

Flip edges to try to modify this initial packing so that first, all circles are white or blue, and second, so that the blue circles are symmetrically spaced at the vertices of a regular dodecahedron. 

Place the mouse on an edge and press 'f'. Move the sphere around with the mouse to see the back.

Good luck. </text>
<cmd name="*" mnemonic="*" tooltip="start over" iconname="icq_dnd.png">act 0;Cleanse;set_display -m .75;infile_read icos1.p;color -c d;Disp -w -cf -f -ec20t8 elist;act 1;infile_read firstOne.p;color -c d;Disp -w -cf -f -ec20t8 elist; </cmd>
<cmd name="r" mnemonic="r" tooltip="create a new random triangulation" iconname="centrejust.png">act 1;random_triangulation -S 42;max_pack;color -c d;Disp -w -cf -f </cmd>
<cmd inline="no" name="f" mnemonic="f" tooltip="pick an edge to 'flip'" iconname="button_ok.png">set_elist z #XY;flip elist[n];max_pack;NSpole;color -c d;disp -wr; </cmd>
<text> The key 'h' when pressed on an edge will establish a 'half-hex' path in the complex, and then pressing '1' will do a flip along that path. </text>
<cmd inline="no" name="h" mnemonic="h" tooltip="shoot a half-hex path" iconname="amarok.png">set_elist z #XY;hh_path elist;disp -w -cf -f -ec20t8 elist; </cmd>
<cmd inline="no" name="1" mnemonic="1" tooltip="flip along the half-hex path" iconname="apollon.png">flip -cw elist[n];max_pack;color -c d;disp -wr;disp -ec20t8 elist; </cmd>
  </CPscript>
